{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
'''Group B of the 1986 FIFA  World Cup''' was one of the groups of nations competing at the [[1986 FIFA World Cup]]. The group's first round of matches began on 3 June and its last matches were played on 11 June. Matches were played at the [[Estadio Azteca]] in [[Mexico City]] and at the [[Estadio Nemesio Díez]] in [[Toluca]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/86full.html |title=World Cup 1986 |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> Host [[Mexico national football team|Mexico]] topped the group, joined in the second round by [[Belgium national football team|Belgium]] and by [[Paraguay national football team|Paraguay]], who were making their first appearance in the finals since 1958. [[Iraq national football team|Iraq]], making their debut in the World Cup, lost all three of their matches and scored just one goal.

